    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`plan_extraction` is implemented in `solution.py`, and all 33 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`. The checks for coverage, CRAP score, mutation score and bandit were not run here, so I can't say whether those gates pass.\n\nThe code splits the work into two small helpers: `_has_drive` checks for a drive prefix, and `_normalise` does the per-member validation and normalisation. `plan_extraction` handles `dest`, skips directory entries and rejects case-insensitive duplicates.\n\nThe tests cover each rule in the spec, including `a:` being rejected as a drive prefix while names like `..a`, `a..`, `1:x` and `é:x` are accepted. They also check that directory entries are validated but not returned or counted as duplicates, and that no partial plan is returned when any member is unsafe.",
